<html xmlns:o='urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:office' xmlns:w='urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:word' xmlns='http://www.w3.org/TR/REC-html40'>
<head>
    <meta charset="utf-8">
    <title>SIH Presentation Guide - Detailed Roadmap</title>
    <style>
        body { font-family: Arial, sans-serif; line-height: 1.6; margin: 40px; color: #333; }
        h1 { color: #2c3e50; border-bottom: 2px solid #3498db; padding-bottom: 10px; }
        h2 { color: #2980b9; margin-top: 30px; border-bottom: 1px solid #ddd; padding-bottom: 5px; }
        h3 { color: #16a085; }
        p { font-size: 14px; margin-bottom: 15px; }
        ul { margin-bottom: 20px; }
        li { font-size: 14px; margin-bottom: 8px; }
        .highlight { background-color: #f1f8ff; border-left: 4px solid #3498db; padding: 15px; margin: 20px 0; font-style: italic; }
        .cred-box { background-color: #fef9e7; border: 1px dashed #f39c12; padding: 10px; display: inline-block; margin-bottom: 15px; font-weight: bold; }
    </style>
</head>
<body>

    <h1>SIH Project Presentation: Complete Step-by-Step Roadmap</h1>
    <p><em>This is your exact roadmap. Follow these steps during your presentation. It tells you exactly what to click, what credentials to use, and what to say to the invigilator for all 4 dashboards.</em></p>

    <div class="highlight">
        <strong>Important Setup:</strong> Before the invigilator arrives, make sure your React frontend is running on <code>localhost:5173</code>, your Node backend on <code>localhost:5000</code>, and your Flask ML engine on <code>localhost:5001</code>. Start at the Login page.
    </div>

    <h2>Introduction (What to say)</h2>
    <p><strong>You say:</strong> "Hello sir/ma'am. We are solving Problem Statement 26134. Today, there is a massive gap between what colleges teach, what students know, and what companies actually need. To solve this, we built a <strong>Data-Driven Curriculum Alignment Platform</strong>. Let me show you how it works for Companies, Colleges, Students, and the Government."</p>

    <!-- COMPANY SECTION -->
    <h2>Step 1: The Company Dashboard (Industry Demand)</h2>
    <div class="cred-box">Login Credentials &rarr; Email: tcs@demo.com | Password: demo123</div>
    
    <p><strong>Action 1:</strong> Go to the login page. Under "Welcome Back", enter the company credentials and click <strong>Sign In</strong>.</p>
    <p><strong>You say:</strong> "First, we log in as a Company (TCS). This is where industry demand starts. Companies use this dashboard for three main things:"</p>
    
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Action 2 (Post Jobs Tab):</strong> Click on the "Post Jobs" tab. <br>
        <strong>You say:</strong> "They post their real hiring requirements. This gives our system live data on exactly which skills are in demand right now."</li>
        
        <li><strong>Action 3 (Industry Consultation Tab):</strong> Click on the "Industry Consultation" tab. <br>
        <strong>You say:</strong> "Companies can also submit formal Industry Consultations. They report what emerging skills they will need in the next 6 to 12 months. This directly helps colleges plan ahead."</li>
        
        <li><strong>Action 4 (Validate Reports Tab):</strong> Click on the "Validate Reports" tab. <br>
        <strong>You say:</strong> "Finally, employers can review a college's updated curriculum and click 'Validate' to confirm if the college is now teaching the right things."</li>
    </ul>
    <p><strong>Action 5:</strong> Click "Logout" at the top right.</p>

    <!-- COLLEGE SECTION -->
    <h2>Step 2: The College Dashboard (Updating Curriculum)</h2>
    <div class="cred-box">Login Credentials &rarr; Email: jiet@demo.com | Password: demo123</div>

    <p><strong>Action 1:</strong> Log in using the College credentials.</p>
    <p><strong>You say:</strong> "Next, we log in as a College. How does a college know what to teach? They upload their current syllabus here, and our smart AI engine instantly generates a <strong>Gap Report</strong>."</p>

    <ul>
        <li><strong>Action 2 (Gap Reports Tab):</strong> Make sure you are on the "Gap Reports" tab. Point to the report on the screen. <br>
        <strong>You say:</strong> "As you can see, the AI reads the job postings we just saw and compares them to the college syllabus. It highlights <strong>Missing Industry Skills</strong> (in red) and warns the college about <strong>Obsolete/Outdated Topics</strong> (like old software versions)."</li>
        
        <li><strong>Action 3 (Mark as Revised):</strong> Scroll to the bottom of a gap report and click the green "✓ Mark Curriculum as Revised" button. <br>
        <strong>You say:</strong> "It also recommends specific courses. Once the college updates their curriculum, they click this button. This creates a digital proof that the college actually took action."</li>
        
        <li><strong>Action 4 (Training Plans Tab):</strong> Click the "Generate District Plan" tab. <br>
        <strong>You say:</strong> "Colleges can also generate automated district-level training plans detailing exact trainer and equipment requirements."</li>
    </ul>
    <p><strong>Action 5:</strong> Click "Logout" at the top right.</p>

    <!-- STUDENT SECTION -->
    <h2>Step 3: The Student Dashboard (Personal Upskilling)</h2>
    <div class="cred-box">Login Credentials &rarr; Email: student@demo.com | Password: demo123</div>

    <p><strong>Action 1:</strong> Log in using the Student credentials.</p>
    <p><strong>You say:</strong> "Now, we log in as a Student. Students are often confused about what to study. Here is how we guide them:"</p>

    <ul>
        <li><strong>Action 2 (Market Skill Gaps Tab):</strong> Look at the High-Demand Missing Skills list. <br>
        <strong>You say:</strong> "They can see a live list of the most high-demand skills that are currently missing in the market, along with recommended courses."</li>
        
        <li><strong>Action 3 (Personal Assessment Tab):</strong> Click on "Personal Assessment". Type "HTML, CSS, Java" in the box and click "Analyze My Skills". <br>
        <strong>You say:</strong> "A student types in their current skills. The AI instantly compares their profile against active job postings and tells them exactly what they are missing to get hired."</li>
        
        <li><strong>Action 4 (Career Pathways Tab):</strong> Click on "Career Pathways". <br>
        <strong>You say:</strong> "They can also see data-driven career pathways to understand how to move from a beginner to an advanced role."</li>
    </ul>
    <p><strong>Action 5:</strong> Click "Logout" at the top right.</p>

    <!-- ADMIN SECTION -->
    <h2>Step 4: The Admin Dashboard (The Big Picture)</h2>
    <div class="cred-box">Login Credentials &rarr; Email: admin@demo.com | Password: demo123</div>

    <p><strong>Action 1:</strong> Log in using the Admin credentials.</p>
    <p><strong>You say:</strong> "Finally, the Government or Admin needs to see the big picture to plan national or district-level training programs."</p>

    <ul>
        <li><strong>Action 2:</strong> Slowly scroll down the Admin Dashboard, pointing out the charts. <br>
        <strong>You say:</strong> "In the Admin Dashboard, they can see everything in one place:"
            <ul>
                <li>"<strong>Sector Growth:</strong> Which sector (like IT or Manufacturing) is growing fastest and generating the most jobs."</li>
                <li>"<strong>Proficiency Demand:</strong> Whether companies need Beginner, Intermediate, or Advanced candidates."</li>
                <li>"<strong>Evidence Quality Indicators:</strong> At the bottom, they can see exactly how many colleges have revised their curriculum and how many have been validated by employers."</li>
            </ul>
        </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Conclusion</h2>
    <p><strong>You say:</strong> "In conclusion, our platform doesn't just show data. It creates a complete, continuous loop: Companies signal demand &rarr; AI analyzes the gap &rarr; Colleges update their syllabus &rarr; Students upskill &rarr; Admin tracks the progress. Thank you!"</p>

</body>
</html>
